  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Natural talent for opening and filling an aperture is graded on a four-step scale from A down to D. C grade sits above D grade and below B grade on that scale. Gu Yue clan talk treats a C grade youth as ordinary investment: after about two years of cultivation the youth usually becomes a rank two senior Gu Master and clan backbone.",
      "chapters": [
        4
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_gu_yue_clan",
        "sys_gu_master"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "On Qing Mao Mountain, the Awakening Ceremony measures talent by how far a fifteen-year-old walks into the moon orchid flower sea while Hope Gu enter the body. Fang Yuan states the bands used there: below ten steps means no cultivation talent, ten to twenty is D grade, twenty to thirty C grade, thirty to forty B grade, and forty to fifty A grade.",
      "chapters": [
        5
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "how-the-grade-is-measured",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_qing_mao_mountain",
        "gu_hope_gu",
        "char_fang_yuan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan walks twenty-three steps and returns as a C grade talent.",
      "chapters": [
        5
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "how-the-grade-is-measured",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "His aperture’s primeval sea sits at forty-four percent of the space, named as the limitation of that grade.",
      "chapters": [
        6
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "how-the-grade-is-measured",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "The result shocks the watching clan: years of genius talk had pointed at an A grade outcome, and his twin Fang Zheng later takes that A grade place instead.",
      "chapters": [
        2
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "how-the-grade-is-measured",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_zheng"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The grade governs how much of the aperture the primeval sea fills, and therefore how much essence the Gu Master holds and how fast that essence recovers.",
      "chapters": [
        7
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "what-c-grade-governs",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "The academy elder states that a C grade talent’s primeval sea takes up four to five layers of the aperture. Progress usually stops at rank two, though with luck a small percentage can advance to rank three initial stage.",
      "chapters": [
        7
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "what-c-grade-governs",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Natural recovery for Fang Yuan’s C grade sea is about four percent of the aperture store per hour, twenty-four percent in six hours, half the natural rate of an A grade talent like Fang Zheng.",
      "chapters": [
        10
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "what-c-grade-governs",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_a_grade"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "That shortfall is why, during the academy’s vital Gu refinement test, a C grade youth must burn primeval stones to hold progress while an A grade youth can keep refining from recovery alone.",
      "chapters": [
        8
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "what-c-grade-governs",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_vital_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Chi Lian later states the same gap as time: rising to middle stage on talent alone usually takes a C grade youth twice as long as a B grade, and four times as long as an A grade.",
      "chapters": [
        50
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "what-c-grade-governs",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Once Fang Yuan’s C grade is public, academy and household talk downgrade him against Fang Zheng’s A grade. Uncle Gu Yue Dong Tu treats the C grade as luck that the household won the stronger twin; Shen Cui’s attention shifts to Fang Zheng for the same reason.",
      "chapters": [
        9
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "academy-and-clan-talk",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_gu_yue_dong_tu",
        "char_shen_cui"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The academy elder decides a C grade who looks broken by the result is not worth heavy fostering beside an A grade sibling.",
      "chapters": [
        7
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "academy-and-clan-talk",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Classmates and branch elders keep calling him a C grade even after he takes first place refining Moonlight Gu, reading the win as luck or a weak Gu will rather than a change of talent.",
      "chapters": [
        21
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "academy-and-clan-talk",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "gu_moonlight_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "In later clan-hall talk, elders still treat a C grade Fang Yuan as worth investing because of his blood link to A grade Fang Zheng, and Gu Yue Bo’s public reward still names the C grade when granting thirty primeval stones for a first-place result.",
      "chapters": [
        78
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "academy-and-clan-talk",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_gu_yue_bo"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Talent grades sit beside the aperture mechanics on aperture and primeval essence. The ceremony that produces the grade is on Awakening Ceremony. The full ladder is on Aptitude.",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "no_citation",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "academy-and-clan-talk",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_aptitude",
        "sys_aperture_and_primeval_essence",
        "sys_awakening_ceremony"
      ]
    }
  ],
